[{:seon.task/name "a-missing-local-root-is-unresolved"
  :seon.task/plan "Reproduction: `jolt.deps/resolve-deps` on `{nowhere/nothing {:local/root \"/tmp/zzmissing\"}}` answers `{:roots [\"/tmp/zzmissing/src\"] :libs {nowhere/nothing {:local/root \"/tmp/zzmissing\"}}}` with no error, because `manifest-info` treats a directory without a deps.edn as a bare source tree without checking it exists, while a missing `:mvn/version` throws `{:unresolved [...]}` through `fail-unresolvable!`. tools.deps refuses a missing :local/root. Correct, in our Jolt fork on a jolt/<topic> branch (a dependency change waits for root's go): `local-info` calls `jolt.deps/note-unresolvable!` when the path does not exist, so `fail-unresolvable!` throws. `seon.fx/resolve-deps` already relies on Jolt alone (no existence check of its own)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.fx-test/a-missing-local-root-fails-in-jolts-resolver}}]
